        "execSummary":  "The indeterminate behavior of AI systems breaks the assumption underlying traditional IT governance: that tested systems behave predictably in production. CIOs who have found the right balance are creating structural separation between innovation teams and compliance functions ΓÇö not as bureaucracy, but as a deliberate tension that accelerates safe experimentation. For customer-support leaders, this model is directly applicable: autonomous AI handling customer interactions must have an independent oversight function that can detect and halt unexpected behavior before it reaches scale. The key risk to watch is shadow AI use, which erodes governance from the inside when official channels are perceived as too slow.",
