        "execSummary":  "Gartner\u0027s Inference Paradox should be a forcing function for every enterprise AI business case: per-token costs are falling, but total inference spend is on track to increase more than fivefold by 2028 because agentic workflows consume dramatically more tokens than chatbots. For customer-support leaders, this means the ROI math for AI-assisted or autonomous support must account for token volume that scales with interaction complexity, not just interaction count. The strategic implication is that cost predictability requires governing agent complexity and chaining depth, not just negotiating model pricing. Organizations that delay building token consumption baselines now will face budget shocks as agentic deployments mature.",
